{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017BnJHta6V46BoF2y7PhD8F","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Literature Map for faith-evidence-ie (FREIGE)\\\\n# Focus: CED-as-training-stabilizer (D024) + RSFT for DocRE\\\\n# Updated: 2026-05-15\\\\n\\\\npapers:\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 1: Reward Diversity / Reward Shaping for RL Stability ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"GDPO: Group reward-Decoupled Normalization Policy Optimization for Multi-reward RL Optimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: NVIDIA Labs\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: ICML 2026\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.05242\\\\n    category: reward_diversity\\\\n    role: closest_prior_work\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      直接将 GRPO 应用于多 reward 组合时，不同 rollout 的 reward 组合在归一化后 collapse 为相同 advantage 值，\\\\n      降低训练信号分辨率导致收敛失败。GDPO 对每个 reward 独立做 group-wise normalization 再聚合，\\\\n      保留多 reward 的相对差异，显著提升训练稳定性。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      最直接相关。CED reward 本质上引入了独立于 extraction F1 的 reward 维度（evidence quality），\\\\n      GDPO 的理论分析解释了为什么多维 reward 比单一 reward 更稳定——独立 reward 维度防止 advantage collapse。\\\\n      但 GDPO 是方法论贡献，CED 是 task-specific reward 设计自然具备了这一特性。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"DRA-GRPO: Exploring Diversity-Aware Reward Adjustment for R1-Zero-Like Training of LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Xiwen Chen et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2505.09655\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.09655\\\\n    category: reward_diversity\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      GRPO 的标量 reward 无法区分语义多样但得分相同的输出（diversity-quality inconsistency）。\\\\n      DRA 用子模互信息（SMI）对 reward 加权，给多样性高的 completion 更大权重，\\\\n      等价于 Inverse Propensity Scoring 去偏，防止 policy 坍缩到先验模式。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      DRA 通过后处理 reward 注入多样性信号；CED 的 reward 本身就内含对比结构自然提供 diversity 信号。\\\\n      机制互补但来源不同——CED 是 reward design 层面，DRA 是 optimization 层面。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Shrinking the Variance: Shrinkage Baselines for RL with Verifiable Rewards\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Guanning Zeng et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2511.03710\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.03710\\\\n    category: reward_diversity\\\\n    role: theoretical_support\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      RLVR 中 per-prompt 均值 baseline 在低 generation 数下估计不准导致高 variance 梯度。\\\\n      用 James-Stein shrinkage 混合 per-prompt 和 cross-prompt 均值，\\\\n      构造可证明更低 variance 的 policy gradient estimator。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      理论支持：reward variance 对 gradient estimation 质量至关重要。\\\\n      CED 的额外 reward 维度提供更丰富的 per-group variance，间接起到 variance 维持效果。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Reward Shaping to Mitigate Reward Hacking in RLHF\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2502.18770\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.18770\\\\n    category: reward_diversity\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      RL reward 应有界且先快速增长后缓慢收敛。系统研究 reward shaping 原则，\\\\n      好的 reward 形状能抑制 reward hacking 并提升训练稳定性。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      CED reward 的 0-1 对比判别结构天然满足有界性，\\\\n      且 evidence quality 的渐进提升符合\\\\\\\"先快后慢\\\\\\\"的 reward shaping 原则。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 2: Mode Collapse Prevention in GRPO/RLHF ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"DAPO: An Open-Source LLM Reinforcement Learning System at Scale\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: ByteDance Seed, Tsinghua AIR\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: NeurIPS 2025\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.14476\\\\n    category: mode_collapse_prevention\\\\n    role: key_baseline\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      Naive GRPO 存在 entropy collapse（policy 熵快速下降→输出同质化）。\\\\n      DAPO 提出 Clip-Higher（放大 importance sampling 上界）和 Dynamic Sampling\\\\n      来对抗 entropy collapse，在 AIME 2024 上超越 DeepSeek-R1-Zero。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      DAPO 从 optimization 技巧角度解决 entropy collapse；CED reward 本身就能防止 mode collapse，\\\\n      无需额外 clip 调整。reward design vs. algorithm trick 的对比。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Dr. GRPO: Removing Optimization Bias in GRPO\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Liu et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: COLM 2025\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.20783\\\\n    category: mode_collapse_prevention\\\\n    role: related_analysis\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      GRPO 的 std 归一化对低 variance 组（全对/全错）给予过高 advantage 权重引入 difficulty bias。\\\\n      Dr. GRPO 移除 std 归一化项消除偏差，在 per-token 基础上表现更优。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      分析了 reward_std→0 时的问题（advantage 异常放大或归零），\\\\n      与我们观察到的 extraction-only reward 下 frac_zero_std→0.8 现象高度一致。\\\\n      CED 通过增加 reward 维度天然维持 reward_std>0，避免了这一 bias。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"GVPO: Group Variance Policy Optimization for LLM Post-Training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: NeurIPS 2025\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.19599\\\\n    category: mode_collapse_prevention\\\\n    role: alternative_framework\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      将 KL 约束 reward 最大化的解析解直接嵌入梯度权重，\\\\n      variance 项自然平衡 exploration 与 exploitation，维持适度 entropy。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      GVPO 的 variance 项机制与 CED 维持 reward variance 的效果功能类似，\\\\n      但 GVPO 是算法层面 implicit regularization，CED 是 reward 层面 explicit structure。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"REINFORCE++: Stabilizing Critic-Free Policy Optimization with Global Advantage Normalization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Jian Hu et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2501.03262\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.03262\\\\n    category: mode_collapse_prevention\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      Prompt-level (local) advantage normalization 导致不准确估计和过拟合。\\\\n      Global batch normalization 提供更稳定、理论无偏的 gradient estimator。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      解决 local normalization 的 variance 问题；CED 从 reward 端增加 variance 来源。\\\\n      两者在不同层面解决同一问题：防止 gradient signal 消失。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"DiverseGRPO: Mitigating Mode Collapse in Image Generation via Diversity-Aware GRPO\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Henglin Liu et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2512.21514\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.21514\\\\n    category: mode_collapse_prevention\\\\n    role: parallel_work\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      图像生成中 GRPO 后期输出同质化。distributional reward modeling（谱聚类+exploratory reward）\\\\n      和 structure-aware regularization 实现 13-18% 语义多样性提升。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      跨域验证了 GRPO mode collapse 的普遍性，distributional reward 思路与 CED 精神相近——\\\\n      都是通过 reward 层面结构化信号维持输出多样性。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Why GRPO Needs Normalization: A Local-Curvature Perspective on Adaptive Gradients\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2601.23135\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.23135\\\\n    category: mode_collapse_prevention\\\\n    role: theoretical_support\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      GRPO 的 reward_std 归一化在温和条件下提供严格优于未归一化 REINFORCE 的收敛速率，\\\\n      收益由 prompt 间平均 reward std 刻画。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      直接理论支撑：reward_std 越大收敛越好。CED 通过 evidence quality 维度维持高 reward_std，\\\\n      从该理论看 CED 的稳定性优势是 reward_std 维持带来的收敛速率优势。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 3: Contrastive Rewards in RL ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Improving Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback Using Contrastive Rewards\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Shen, Zhang et al.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2403.07708\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07708\\\\n    category: contrastive_reward\\\\n    role: closest_contrastive_precedent\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      Contrastive reward 让 LLM 惩罚 reward uncertainty、改善鲁棒性、\\\\n      根据任务难度自适应校准、减少 PPO 中的 variance。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      最接近的对比 reward 先例。但针对 RLHF 通用场景，\\\\n      CED 是 task-specific evidence discrimination 对比信号，且在 GRPO（非 PPO）中验证。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Improving Discriminative Capability of Reward Models in RLHF Using Contrastive Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: EMNLP 2024\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2024.emnlp-main.852/\\\\n    category: contrastive_reward\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      无监督对比损失训练 reward model 充分捕捉对比数据区分度，\\\\n      带来更稳定的 PPO 训练 return 和 reward。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      验证对比训练 reward model → 更稳定 RL 训练链条。CED 不是对比训练 reward model，\\\\n      而是 reward function 本身就是对比判别，但 stabilizing 机制相通。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Contrastive Preference Learning: Learning from Human Feedback without RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2025\\\\n    url: https://openreview.net/forum?id=iX1RjVQODj\\\\n    category: contrastive_reward\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      将 preference learning 重新表述为对比学习问题，无需显式 RL 即可从人类反馈中学习。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      对比框架在 preference alignment 中的通用性。CED 可被视为 task-specific contrastive preference signal。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 4: Evidence-Based Rewards in IE/NLP ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Drift: Enhancing LLM Faithfulness in Rationale Generation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: ACL 2025\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.340.pdf\\\\n    category: evidence_reward\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      用 faithfulness reward 引导 LLM 生成更可靠的 rationale，提升 CoT 推理事实一致性。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      Faithfulness reward 用于生成质量的先例。CED 中 evidence discrimination\\\\n      本质上也是 faithfulness 信号——判断证据是否忠实支持抽取结果。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Fine-Grained NLI-Based Faithfulness Evaluation for Diverse Summarisation Tasks (INFUSE)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: EACL 2024\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.102/\\\\n    category: evidence_reward\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      变长前提+简化假设的细粒度 NLI faithfulness 评估，超越传统 NLI 在多任务摘要上的表现。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      NLI 作为 faithfulness 评估工具的进展。CED 中 NLI 组件用于判断 evidence 对 triple 的支持度。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Enhancing Cross-Evidence Reasoning Graph for Document-Level Relation Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: PMC/Bioinformatics 2024\\\\n    url: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11232587/\\\\n    category: evidence_reward\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      文档级关系抽取中用 cross-evidence reasoning graph 增强跨证据推理。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      DocRE 中 evidence 的重要性。但用 evidence 作为模型输入特征，\\\\n      我们用 evidence quality 作为 RL reward 信号——定位根本不同。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 5: Multi-Objective RL for Text Generation ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Confronting Reward Model Overoptimization with Constrained RLHF\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: OpenReview\\\\n    url: https://openreview.net/forum?id=gkfUvn0fLU\\\\n    category: multi_objective_rl\\\\n    role: related_analysis\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      多组件 RM 的 overoptimization 研究。component RM 间的相关性显著影响 overoptimization 临界点，\\\\n      用 constrained MDP 防止超出适当边界。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      CED 引入了与 extraction F1 低相关的 reward component（evidence quality），\\\\n      根据该论文分析低相关多组件 reward 更不易 overoptimize，\\\\n      可能是 CED 稳定性的另一个理论解释角度。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"On-Policy RL with Optimal Reward Baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2505.23585\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.23585\\\\n    category: multi_objective_rl\\\\n    role: theoretical_support\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      Optimal baseline 一致性地实现更高训练 reward 和更高 entropy，\\\\n      有效稳定训练并促进更多样的 policy exploration。\\\\n    relevance_to_ced_stabilizer: >\\\\n      CED reward 的多维特性可能起到类似 optimal baseline 效果——\\\\n      evidence quality 维度为 advantage estimation 提供更丰富的参照信号。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 6: RSFT Methodology & Theory ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"A Minimalist Approach to LLM Reasoning: from Rejection Sampling to Reinforce\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Xiao et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2504.11343\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11343\\\\n    category: rsft_methodology\\\\n    role: key_theoretical_support\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      RAFT（简单 rejection sampling baseline）在数学推理上与 GRPO/PPO 表现相当。\\\\n      消融实验表明 GRPO 的主要优势来自丢弃全错 prompt 而非 reward normalization。\\\\n      提出 Reinforce-Rej，在 RAFT 基础上过滤全对和全错 sample。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      直接支持我们的设计选择：RSFT 在 DocRE 上成功而 GRPO 失败的原因可能是\\\\n      structured output（DocRE）比 math reasoning 更难用 online RL 优化，\\\\n      而 rejection sampling 的 offline 特性天然避免了 catastrophic forgetting。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Beyond Rejection Sampling: Trajectory Fusion for Scaling Mathematical Reasoning (TrajFusion)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Jie Deng et al.\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2602.04391\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.04391\\\\n    category: rsft_methodology\\\\n    role: method_component\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      传统 RSFT 只用正确轨迹，丢弃错误轨迹。TrajFusion 将错误和正确轨迹交替拼接，\\\\n      显式建模试错推理过程，在困难数学问题上显著超越标准 RFT。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      Future work 方向：可考虑在 DocRE RSFT 中融合失败样本的信息。\\\\n      但 DocRE 的结构化输出（JSON triple）不同于 math 的 chain-of-thought，\\\\n      融合方式需要重新设计。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Rejection Sampling Based Fine Tuning Secretly Performs PPO\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: ICML 2025\\\\n    url: https://openreview.net/forum?id=yQ2UivKlir\\\\n    category: rsft_methodology\\\\n    role: theoretical_support\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      建立 RSFT 与 PPO 之间的理论联系：rejection sampling fine-tuning\\\\n      在特定条件下隐式执行 PPO with marginal KL constraints。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      为 RSFT 的有效性提供理论解释。我们的 RSFT 成功可被视为\\\\n      隐式执行了 constrained policy optimization，\\\\n      避免了显式 GRPO 在 structured output 上的不稳定性。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 7: RL for Information Extraction ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"R1-RE: Cross-Domain Relation Extraction with RLVR\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Runpeng Dai, Tong Zheng et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2507.04642\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.04642\\\\n    category: rl_for_ie\\\\n    role: direct_competitor\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      首个将 RLVR（GRPO + verifiable reward）用于关系抽取的框架。\\\\n      将 RE 重构为推理任务，R1-RE-7B 在跨域 OOD 准确率约 70%，\\\\n      媲美 GPT-4o。在 SemEval-2010 Task 8 和私有 MDKG 数据集上评估。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      最直接竞争者。但关键差异：(1) R1-RE 是句子级 RE，我们是文档级 RE；\\\\n      (2) R1-RE 用 online GRPO，我们用 offline RSFT；\\\\n      (3) R1-RE 无 evidence extraction 组件，我们有 CED reward；\\\\n      (4) R1-RE 关注 OOD 泛化，我们关注 evidence-grounded extraction quality。\\\\n      互补而非直接冲突。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"MORE-R1: Guiding LVLM for Multimodal Object-Entity Relation Extraction via Stepwise Reasoning with RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2603.09478\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.09478\\\\n    category: rl_for_ie\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      多模态 RE 中用 GRPO + Progressive Sample-Mixing Strategy 优化 LVLM 推理能力。\\\\n      两阶段训练：SFT cold-start + GRPO RL。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      跨模态验证 RL for RE 趋势。其 Progressive Sample-Mixing 与我们\\\\n      RSFT 的 difficulty-aware sampling 思想相通，但在不同模态。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"REAR: Reinforced Reasoning Optimization for Event Argument Extraction with Relation-Aware Support\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Jianwen Luo et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: EMNLP 2025 Findings\\\\n    url: https://2025.emnlp.org/program/find_papers/\\\\n    category: rl_for_ie\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      将强化学习推理优化用于事件论元抽取，结合关系感知支持。\\\\n      不同于 DocRE 但同属 IE 领域的 RL 应用。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      验证 RL 在 IE 任务上的有效性趋势。我们的工作扩展到 DocRE + evidence，\\\\n      且使用 offline RSFT 而非 online RL。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Adaptive Reinforcement Learning Planning: Harnessing LLMs for Complex Information Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Zepeng Ding et al.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2406.11455\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.11455\\\\n    category: rl_for_ie\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      将 LLM 顺序抽取建模为 MDP，用 DDQN 训练 decision module\\\\n      自适应选择实体抽取顺序，提升复杂 IE 性能。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      RL for IE 的早期工作。用 RL 优化抽取策略而非模型本身，\\\\n      与我们 RSFT 直接微调 LLM 的方法路径不同。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Graph-R1: Towards Agentic GraphRAG Framework via End-to-end Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Haoran Luo et al.\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: ICML 2026\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.21892\\\\n    category: rl_for_ie\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      用端到端 RL 优化 GraphRAG agent 的多轮检索-推理循环，\\\\n      包含 knowledge hypergraph construction（n-ary relation extraction）。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      RL + knowledge extraction 的交叉点。Graph-R1 关注 QA 场景下的知识图谱构建，\\\\n      我们关注 DocRE 的训练优化，应用场景不同。\\\\n\\\\n  # === Category 8: Recent LLM-based DocRE Methods ===\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"RelPrior: Relation as a Prior - A Novel Paradigm for LLM-based Document-level Relation Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2511.08143\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.08143\\\\n    category: llm_docre\\\\n    role: key_baseline\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      用 binary relation 作为先验过滤无关实体对，再用 predefined relation 匹配实体，\\\\n      避免 LLM 在 DocRE 中被无关实体对分散注意力。\\\\n      在 DocRED/Re-DocRED 上超越现有 LLM-based DocRE 方法。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      我们的直接 baseline 之一。RelPrior 在 DocRED 上提升 +2.06-2.38pp，\\\\n      我们的 RSFT 提升 +5.98pp 显著更优。\\\\n      RelPrior 是 inference paradigm 创新，我们是 training paradigm 创新，正交互补。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"LMRC: LLM with Relation Classifier for Document-Level Relation Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2408.13889\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.13889\\\\n    category: llm_docre\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      两阶段方法：先用 attention-based classifier 过滤 NA 实体对（RCP），\\\\n      再用 LLM 在精简候选空间中做多分类（RC）。\\\\n      在 DocRED/Re-DocRED 上显著优于其他 LLM-based DocRE 方法。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      LMRC 用小模型预筛选 + LLM 分类的 pipeline 方式，与我们端到端 LLM 生成方式不同。\\\\n      展示 LLM-based DocRE 的 class imbalance 挑战，我们通过 RSFT 的 reward-based filtering 隐式解决。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"Ru-LLM: Logical Rule-Constrained Large Language Models for Document-Level Relation Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: NLPCC 2025\\\\n    url: https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-95-3343-5_11\\\\n    category: llm_docre\\\\n    role: related_method\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      用频繁模式挖掘 + MCTS 搜索逻辑规则，转化为 prompt 约束 LLM 输出，\\\\n      再用 CoT 验证过滤不满足规则的 triple。\\\\n      在 DWIE、DocRED、Re-DocRED 上超越现有 LLM 方法和规则框架。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      规则约束方式与我们的 CED reward 在 motivation 上相似（都是引入外部知识约束），\\\\n      但 Ru-LLM 用 inference-time 规则验证，我们用 training-time reward shaping。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"GLiDRE: Generalist Lightweight model for Document-level Relation Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2508.00757\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.00757\\\\n    category: llm_docre\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      基于 dual-encoder 的轻量级零/少样本 DocRE 模型，\\\\n      在 Re-DocRED、FREDo 等 benchmark 的 few-shot 场景达到 SOTA。\\\\n      预训练于 136K 文档的大规模 RE 数据。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      不同范式（encoder-based vs LLM generative），\\\\n      但验证了 DocRE 领域仍有方法创新空间。\\\\n\\\\n  - title: \\\\\\\"AutoRE: Document-Level Relation Extraction with Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: Anonymous\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: arXiv 2403.14888\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.14888\\\\n    category: llm_docre\\\\n    role: background\\\\n    key_finding: >\\\\n      RHF（Relation-Head-Facts）范式用 Mistral-7B + QLoRA 做端到端 DocRE，\\\\n      在多个 LLM 上达到 SOTA。\\\\n    relevance_to_rsft_docre: >\\\\n      QLoRA fine-tuning for DocRE 的先例。我们的 SFT baseline 与之类似，\\\\n      RSFT 在此基础上引入 reward-guided sample selection 进一步提升。\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 17868, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NP9Y11DQpg1pHPZ263S9Gi","session_id":"6f25cfed-835a-4517-9646-6292208db176","uuid":"953da63f-1fff-402b-9490-20c476222526","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:10:08.750Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019XtkprzzZA8Vpp8r9pdHnr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W9UqwyL8aJV3AUpwvgEPBC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus areas are **Novelty** and **Related Work**. Produce a blind, independent review. Do NOT speculate about whether the paper will be accepted or rejected — just evaluate objectively.\n\n## Venue: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ACL Rolling Review)\n\n### Scoring scales:\n- **Soundness** (1-5): 5=Excellent (most thorough), 4=Strong (sufficient for all claims), 3=Acceptable (sufficient for main claims), 2=Poor (main claims not supported), 1=Major issues\n- **Excitement** (1-5): 5=Highly exciting, 4=Exciting, 3=Interesting, 2=Potentially interesting, 1=Not exciting\n- **Overall Assessment** (1-5, 0.5 increments): 5=Award, 4.5=Borderline award, 4=Conference accept, 3.5=Borderline conference, 3=Findings, 2.5=Borderline findings, 2=Resubmit next cycle, 1.5=Resubmit after next, 1=Do not resubmit\n- **Reproducibility** (1-5): 5=Easily reproduce, 4=Mostly reproduce, 3=With some difficulty, 2=Hard pressed, 1=Cannot reproduce\n- **Confidence** (1-5): 5=Positive evaluation correct, 4=Quite sure, 3=Pretty sure, 2=Fairly likely missed details, 1=Not my area\n\n### EMNLP typical acceptance rate: ~25% main conference, ~40% including Findings\n\n---\n\n## Paper: FREIGE: Faithful Evidence Generation for LLM-Based Document-Level Relation Extraction via Contrastive Evidence Discrimination\n\n### Abstract\nLLMs are closing the gap with encoder-based methods on document-level relation extraction (DocRE), yet no existing LLM approach produces verifiable evidence. FREIGE is the first generative LLM framework jointly outputting relation triples and explicit sentence-level evidence citations on DocRED. Core: CED (Contrastive Evidence Discrimination) scoring via entailment gap between gold evidence and best entity-sharing distractor. Key findings: naïve NLI scoring fooled by entity-sharing distractors; online RL (GRPO+QLoRA) catastrophic forgetting; CED-guided RSFT yields +5.5pp rel_F1, +1.7pp Evi-F1, −7.1pp EDCR on test. Also proposes EDCR metric (human r=0.62).\n\n### Introduction (Section 1)\n- DocRE requires identifying relational facts between entity pairs spanning multiple sentences\n- Encoder-based methods achieve strong extraction with implicit evidence (attention thresholding)\n- LLM approaches show competitive extraction but produce NO explicit evidence — gap for deployment in KB population, biomedical curation, RAG provenance\n- Entity-sharing distractor sentences get spuriously high NLI scores due to lexical overlap\n- Online RL (GRPO) causes catastrophic forgetting with evidence-extraction decoupling\n- Three contributions: CED scoring, CED-guided RSFT, EDCR metric\n\n### Related Work (Section 2)\n**Document-Level RE:**\n- Encoder-based: DREEAM (RoBERTa-large, attention evidence, Evi-F1_J=0.573), SAIS (Evi-F1_J=0.557)\n- LLM-based: LMRC (LLaMA-3.1-8B, F1=60.69, no evidence)\n- FREIGE bridges gap: joint triples + explicit evidence\n\n**Reward Hacking and Overoptimization:**\n- Connects to RLHF overoptimization literature\n- CED as anti-overoptimization mechanism for evidence grounding\n\n**Rejection Sampling Fine-Tuning:**\n- RSFT theoretically equivalent to PPO under certain conditions\n- Applied here to evidence-grounded IE domain\n\n### Method (Section 3)\n**CED:** Contrastive margin = p_entail(gold) − max(p_entail(distractor from entity-sharing non-gold sentences)). Uses DeBERTa-v3-base on MNLI.\n\n**RSFT Pipeline:** SFT → Generate N=8 candidates → CED filter top-1 → fine-tune on filtered data (~2,718 from 21,952 candidates)\n\n**EDCR metric:** Proportion of cited sentences that are entity-sharing but non-gold evidence.\n\n### Experiments (Section 4)\n**Test set (Table 1):** FREIGE rel_F1=0.455, Evi-F1_J=0.376, EDCR=0.648. SFT baseline: 0.400/0.322/0.719. LMRC (no evidence): 0.607. DREEAM: Evi-F1_J=0.573.\n\n**RL spectrum (Table 3):** GRPO G=4 rel_F1=0.014, G=8=0.031; DPO=0.325; SFT=0.406; RSFT+CED=0.468\n\n**CED vs flat-NLI (Table 4):** CED > flat-NLI by +2.71pp rel_F1 (p<0.01)\n\n**CED modes (Table 5):** Training (RSFT) >> Inference (reranker) for rel_F1\n\n**EDCR diagnostic (Table 6):** Gradient from GRPO(0.988) to CED-reranker(0.598). EDCR-EviF1 Pearson r=−0.42.\n\n**Human validation (Table 7):** 100 samples, 3 annotators, κ=0.72, Pearson r=0.62.\n\n**Model scale (Table 8):** 1.7B (+3.12pp), 4B (+6.26pp), 8B (+4.89pp) — consistent.\n\n**Re-DocRED (Table 9):** Delta preserved (+5.55pp).\n\n**top_k ablation (Table 10):** k=1 > k=3.\n\n**NLI ablation (Table 11):** DeBERTa-base vs large: +0.38pp, marginal.\n\n**Evidence baselines (Table 12):** FREIGE Evi-F1_J=0.381 vs DREEAM=0.572. Gap from extraction accuracy not evidence quality: conditional Evi-F1 0.807 vs 0.834.\n\n### Discussion (Section 5)\n- Why RSFT succeeds: avoids credit assignment issues, QLoRA parameter overwriting, asymmetric gradient optimization\n- EDCR limitations: entity-sharing is proxy, +6.8pp auto-human bias, doesn't capture non-entity-sharing distractors\n- Extraction gap vs encoders: rel_F1 0.455 vs ~0.631 DREEAM, inherent to generative paradigm at current scale\n\n---\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nFocus on **Novelty** and **Related Work**. Evaluate:\n\n1. **Novelty assessment**: How novel are the three contributions (CED, CED-RSFT, EDCR)? Are they incremental combinations of existing techniques or genuinely new ideas?\n2. **Related work coverage**: Are important baselines and related methods missing? Is the positioning accurate?\n3. **Claim of \"first\"**: The paper claims to be the \"first LLM-based DocRE with explicit evidence.\" Is this claim justified? Could there be concurrent or prior work doing similar things?\n4. **Framing and positioning**: Is the narrative fair? Does the paper oversell or undersell its contributions? Is the comparison with encoder methods fair?\n5. **Broader impact and significance**: How significant is this work for the NLP community? Does it open new research directions?\n6. **Writing quality and presentation**: Is the paper clearly written? Are there structural issues?\n\n## Output Format\n\nProduce your review in this exact format:\n\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty & Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentence summary]\n\n### Strengths\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n- S3: ...\n[etc.]\n\n### Weaknesses\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n- W3: ...\n[etc.]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n- Q1: ...\n- Q2: ...\n[etc.]\n\n### Missing Related Work / Positioning Issues\n- P1: ...\n[etc.]\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Excitement: X/5\n- Overall: X.X/5\n- Reproducibility: X/5\n- Confidence: X/5\n\n### Justification for Overall Score\n[2-3 sentences]\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":714,"cache_read_input_tokens":73134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":714},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f25cfed-835a-4517-9646-6292208db176","uuid":"da557392-a260-4288-84e1-cc8d3d7bfea4"}
